The edge cases from the JSON are now a separate deliverable, json_edge_cases.csv: one line per affected entry with its CUI, label, formula and the reason it is an edge case. It has 20 edge case types covering 1,442 of the 1,499 entries; an entry can appear under more than one type.

1. Entries that are not lookback windows

Counts in this group come from keyword rules, so they are approximate.

No.	Edge case	Entries	Example
1a	Lab challenge / specimen timing	877	“2 hours post 75 g glucose PO”
1b	Dosing / repeat frequency	111	“Every four hours”, “Every five years”
1c	Gestational / postpartum	67	“Gestation period, 32 weeks”
1d	Age band	48	“55-59”, “65+”, “Under 5 Years Old”
1e	Duration	34	“1-5 hours each day”, “5-6½ hours”
1f	Survey question with a window inside	24	“I tried to commit suicide in last W”
1g	Billing / admin	21	“Net 30 days”, “Global period 90 days”, “7 day report”
1h	Bare unit	16	“day”, “month”, “Microsecond”
1i	Count of days	10	“12-14 days (nearly every day)”
1j	Anchored to another event	7	“Within thirty days of surgery”
1k	Future-facing	1	“Life expectancy is greater than 6 months”
2. Encoding problems that change the meaning
No.	Edge case	Entries	Example
2a	“More than” / “at least” stored as a single point	66	“More than 5 years” is [5Y, 5Y]
2b	Zero-width at zero	2	“None of the days (0 days)”, “Global period 0 days”
2c	Range that excludes the recent period	187	“13-24 months ago”, “More than 30 days ago but within the past 12 months”
2d	Mixed units in one formula	11	“More than 30 days ago but within the past 12 months” is [30D, 12M]
2e	Labels that differ only by a symbol or decimal point	40	“<2 years” / “2 years” / “> 2 years”; “2.6 hours post” / “26 hours post”
3. Data errors in the file

There are six entries:

“Microsecond” is stored as 1 millisecond.
“More than Half the Days” is stored as half a day.
“Months 1-3 (first trimester)” starts at month 1, not 0.
“1 - 3” and “5 - 9” have no unit, and years are assumed.
“Every four hours” is stored as [0, 4H], while “Every Four to Five Hours” is [4H, 5H].
4. Boundary and precision cases
No.	Edge case	Entries	Example
4a	Month and year length	112	“1 year” misses ≤ 12 months if a year is counted as 365.25 days
4b	Sub-day window	950	“30 minutes”, “Within 24 hours” is the limit
4c	Longer than 10 years	45	Mostly age bands; also “Sixteen to Twenty Years”

The file can be filtered by the no column to pull the full list for any one type.
